x86_64 INTEL INSTRUCTIONS: 
MOV- mov r15, 89 (puts that value of 89 and overwrites the current value of r15)
PUSH- push r15 (places the vaule of r15 into the stack)
POP- pop r8 (removes the vaule of r8 from the stack)
INC- inc r8 (adds 1 from the current value that is at r8)
DEC- dec r8 (subtracts 1 from the current value that is at r8)
ADD- add r13, 69 (adds vaule of r13 and 69 and overwrites the current vaule r13 wit the new vaule)
SUB- sub r13, 10 (subtracts vaule of r13 and 10 and overwrites the current vaule r13 wit the new vaule)
CMP- cmp r10, r7 (compares the vaules of both r10 and r7 through subtraction)
JMP- jmp MEM1 (jump to the memory label MEM1 within the code)
*JMP uses all logical operators JG(jump if greater), JL(jump if less), JNE(jump if not equal), JE(jump equal), JGE(jump greater than or eaqual), JLE(jump less than or equal)*

POP (to take the most recently inserted vaule out of the stack and deleting the vaule from the stack) decerments
PUSH (puts the value into the stack, retaing the value from its source) increments


